# Newsletter → consumer weekly blog (Mejor Vida)

When building or updating a **public weekly blog** from Julie’s newsletter / industry briefing:

1. Follow **`tools/newsletter-to-consumer-blog-prompt.md`** and **`tools/blog-build-rules.md`** (anti-regression checklist §4).
2. Weekly URL = **condensed digest** (150–250 words per story), not the full article.
3. Each digest story: image + headline → fresh summary → CTA to a **separate** full-article page.
4. Full articles = **email-draft length (~600–900 words)**, rewritten for families — not a short teaser and not a paste of the digest. Include FAQ + pillar internal links + bottom **Fuentes / Sources** box with live **primary-authority** URLs (FTC, NFDA, III, BLS, `.gov`, major press — not unknown blogs or vendor sites; no self-only citations; cut unsourced claims).
5. **Never** address agents / IMOs / BGAs / producers on public pages. Topics: **final expense, term life, whole life** for families — Spanish indexed, English `noindex`.
6. Keep SEO assets; strip prior-week schema/hreflang/preload leftovers when cloning templates.
7. Mirror ES ↔ EN structure. **Index Spanish only** (`sitemap.xml` ES URLs; EN `noindex, follow`). No `hreflang` from ES to noindex EN. Do not sitemap/`index` off-topic archive weeks.
